n Man was  released in 2008 it was a smashing  success making about 600 million dollars  globally after decades of bad decisions  bad luck and finally a stroke of success  starting with blade the door to the MCU  finally opened so aside from being  Marvel's first successful film how do we  qualify blades legacy on the MCU and the  superhero genre the most obvious example  is probably in blades world building  which we've already highlighted in this  video four blade gore dreamt up a  compelling and at times totally bonkers  world that ran parallel to ours nearly  every film in the MCU even the most  literal spaced-out ones like guardians  of the galaxy relied on this approach to  deliver a sense of relatability to the  audience you're from Earth Missouri  yeah that's on earth Duke even x-men  which followed blade and is often  considered to be the film that ushered  in the modern era of superhero movies  took that page at a blades book blade  also showed more generally that comics  told genuinely great stories and that if  approached with some degree of  relatability a film about a vampire  slaying half vampire could absolutely  function as a summer blockbuster in  terms of casting blade was revolutionary  in that blade himself was tailored to  fit Snipes persona and strengths not the  other way around  in fact when blade himself debuted in  1973 in tomb of Dracula number 10  his original character was a far cry  from the one portrayed in the film  Wesley Snipes is blade much in the same  way that Robert Downey jr. is Iron Man  the way that writers approach both  characters has forever been changed by  the way both actors molded the character  around themselves and we would be remiss  to overlook blades role and  representation on screen for black  actors when Black Panther was released  in 2018 it was lauded rightfully so for  its nearly all black cast and crew but  many were quick to point out that this  was not the first successful black led  superhero film with 